Ladybird rasters a composited iframe too large to raster whole only
around the part its parent shows, at full scale. Chrome 158, Firefox
151, and WebKit 26.5, run headless, show a 100000px-wide iframe as
sharp as a 360px one. Each rasters only tiles near the visible area:
Chrome’s PictureLayerTiling::ComputeTilePriorityRects() limits live
tiles to an interest rect around the visible rect, WebKit’s
TileController::adjustTileCoverageRect() covers a rect around the
visible one, and WebRender’s TileCacheInstance::pre_update() picks
the picture-cache tiles to raster from the visible region.
